ed in studying and studying more  so the next step for this um kind of  study  will be to um assess the differences not  across biopsies  but across the various glomeruli and  tubules  which was the main initial reason why we  did  we use this technology to start with  and as a step further we use the  computational  um so the question is are there  differences across cells  within a single glomerulus and to answer  this question we use a computational  strategy  to make a deconvolution of the cells  that are present in each glomeruli  and in each tubal that we selected in  our region of  interest so using this computational  algorithm  we were able initially to define  differences  in the cell company composition between  glomeruli and tubules  which was expected but was kind of our  control that this algorithm was working  just fine  and here just by looking at the  composition  um sorry of the different um cells  in the glomeruli and tubules we were  able to identify for example  in the glomeruli some cell subset that  we're not really um  expected to be part of the glomeruli  and similarly so in the in the tube  and if we just look at the composition  of the different cell subset in the  glomeruli  and in the tubules we were able to  identify already some  differences across the different um  across the different  biopsies and and this was true  for the glomeruli as well as  for the for the tubals  so the next step here will be  to assess the gene expression profile  not just in each glomeruli but in each  cell subset within  a single glomerulus which is expected to  give  us important information about the  variability  across the different glomeruli and  understand whether glomeruli that have  similar histological feature have a  similar transcriptional profile  or vice versa if um grameoli  that look different have uh similar  um transcriptional um pathways that are  activated  so that's will be um we believe  um very important to better understand  the molecular mechanisms  that are responsible for the renal  disease progression  and um finally to um  together with the transcriptional  profile  we also tested the protein expression  profile  uh within the kidney so the same slides  slides actually serial slides were also  stained  for different um markers protein markers  and the the purpose of this staining was  to on one hand validate  the the transcriptional profile so that  if we saw  upregulated gene we could confirm that  also the protein were upregulated  but was the other idea was also  to define um  to better define the single structure in  the  in the in the kidney based on the the  expression marker  that um could allow us to identify  um regions in smaller regions of  of interest and to test their their  profile within these regions  and these are the preliminary data that  we  obtained so far with this um with this  technique  where there are many proteins of these  um  panels that are not really over or  underexpressed but there  are two subsets of proteins that are um  um  express highly express or express  um or um or express  or lowly express that will be um  informative to better understand um  and integrate the transcriptional  profile data  so um overall to um to conclude and  summarize our data  we observed differences between alport  fsgs and membranous glomeruli  as well as between glomeruli and tubals  within each disease  we found that not all glomeruli or  tubules are affected in the same way  even within the same kidney and the  spatial profile  can clearly help us understanding such  differences  it also seems that males and females are  often  um affected with ckd different  differently and this  was clearly observed in our outport and  fsgs samples  this could be attributed by the the  variability across samples but could  actually be something that is really sex  dependent  so understanding their differences at  transcriptional level  and also at the protein level could lead  to more specific and personalized  therapies  so um in conclusion the spatial  profiling of gene expression  and we think is a powerful tool that  will allow us to answer some very  important question  about the mechanism of disease  progression in glomerular lckd  such as alport fsgs and membranous  nephropathy  thank you for your attention
 

